2026-10-16 13:04:43 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-16 13:04:43 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent', 'active_learning_agent'], 'text': 'result from master_classifier_repository_agent\nI am the governed system of record for the pinned Master Data Classifiers ruleset (PII/PHI category hierarchy, regex patterns, NER types, confidence thresholds). Before answering, I attempted to read my authoritative stores to cite a pinned revision and check for any HITLGate-related definitions; the store paths are outside the currently allow-listed read scope, so I cannot cite a revision identifier in this pass.\n\nFrom the ruleset I hold, I can confirm the classification-side boundary: the Master Data Classifiers ruleset governs detectable spans and the confidence thresholds at which a span is flagged sensitive — it contains no definitions for page segmentation, page_ids, page_hashes, or chunking. Page-unit production and identity are therefore upstream of, and outside, the classifier definitions the HITLGate would consume. The authoritative statement of what the HITLGate component itself produces versus consumes must come from that component\'s specification or owning agent.\n\n{\n    "Name": "MasterDataClassifiersRuleset",\n    "Inquiry": "Confirm HITLGate scope: does it produce page_ids/page_hashes or perform chunking, or only consume an already-chunked page unit for human review?",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 6,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "Confirmation from the HITLGate component specification or its owning agent on whether it emits page_ids/page_hashes or performs chunking",\n        "An allow-listed read path to the pinned ruleset store so I can cite the exact pinned revision identifier supporting the classifier-side boundary statement"\n    ]\n}'}
