2026-10-16 13:05:15 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-16 13:05:15 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent'], 'text': 'result from feedback_logging_agent\n## My Part of the Answer (Feedback Logging Stage)\n\nHere is my part, plus what my down-chain agent contributed.\n\n**From my boundary (Feedback Logging stage):**\nEverything that reaches me does so *through* the page review gate. Concretely, my records carry a `page_id` field defined as a **deterministic identifier of the page the edit belongs to**. I consume that identifier as an **already-resolved attribute arriving with the edit** — I neither compute it, hash it, nor chunk the page into sub-units. So from my vantage point the HITLGate presents human reviewers with an **already-chunked/identified page unit**, and my job is only to append the resulting ADD/REMOVE/REJECT edits as structured training signal.\n\n**What is outside my observability:**\nWhether the HITLGate itself *originates* `page_ids`/`page_hashes` or performs the chunking step is upstream of me. I only see the fields that survive into the edit record; I cannot confirm where the `page_id` is minted or whether hashing/chunking is a HITLGate responsibility or a distinct upstream component\'s.\n\n**From my down-chain agent (Active Learning Agent):**\nIt reports **not relevant** to defining HITLGate\'s page identification, chunking, or page-unit responsibilities; its authority is limited to the active-learning loop (aggregating APPROVE/MODIFY/REJECT feedback into per-classifier error patterns and staging inert proposals). It also states its own down-chain (Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Authority) reports **no relevance**, covering pinned rulesets only. Both recommend routing this to the component that owns HITLGate\'s page-unit handling.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "Feedback Logging Stage",\n    "Inquiry": "Confirm HITLGate scope: does it produce page_ids/page_hashes or perform chunking, or only consume an already-chunked page unit for human review?",\n    "Mode": "Fulfill",\n    "Response": "Partial. From the feedback-logging boundary: the HITLGate hands the review flow a page unit that is already identified — every edit record I persist arrives with a pre-existing, deterministic page_id, and I neither generate page_ids/page_hashes nor perform chunking. So relative to my stage, the gate consumes/presents an already-chunked, identified page unit for human review. The question of whether the HITLGate itself ORIGINATES page_ids/page_hashes or owns the chunking step is upstream of my observability and cannot be confirmed from the edits alone. My down-chain Active Learning Agent reports Not Relevant (its scope is the active-learning loop only), and its own down-chain (Master Data Classifiers Ruleset Authority) concurs. Definitive confirmation of HITLGate\'s page identification/chunking responsibilities must come from the component that owns HITLGate\'s page-unit handling; I would need that component\'s interface contract (HITLGate -> feedback buffer) to close the boundary."\n}\n```\n\n**Routing note:** The definitive answer on whether HITLGate *produces* `page_ids`/`page_hashes` or *performs chunking* lies with the HITLGate/upstream page-unit owner, not with this feedback-logging chain. What I can confirm from my side is that the gate\'s output to me is an already-identified page unit.'}
