2026-10-16 13:05:17 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-16 13:05:17 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'ingestion_pagination_agent', 'classification_detection_agent', 'redaction_rendering_agent'], 'text': 'result from hitl_gateway_agent\nThis inquiry concerns my own scope, so I can answer directly. I gathered input from my down-chain Feedback Logging agent, and I\'m the component that owns the HITLGate page-unit handling, so I can close the boundary it flagged as upstream.\n\n**Answer:** I only **consume an already-chunked page unit**. I do not produce `page_ids`/`page_hashes` and I do not perform chunking.\n\nMy boundary is as follows:\n- **Input I accept:** a single, already-delineated page unit carrying its `page_id`, `page_number`, and `total_pages` (already resolved upstream). I do not mint, hash, or derive those identifiers.\n- **What I do:** assemble the deterministic side-by-side review payload for that one page unit, transition to `WAITING_FOR_HUMAN`, halt, and capture the human decision.\n- **What I do NOT do:** no page identification/`page_hash` generation, no document chunking/segmentation, no detection, redaction, or learning.\n- **Output consumers use:** `page_id` exactly as supplied, plus the recorded decision (`reviewer_id`, `timestamp`, `action`, `spans_final`) written to the approval_matrix.\n\nSo the authoritative scope statement is: the gate **does not originate page_ids/page_hashes and does not chunk**; it **requires** an upstream component to supply the already-chunked, identified page unit.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "HITL Gate",\n    "Inquiry": "Follow-up: Confirm scope — can HITLGate produce page_ids/page_hashes or perform chunking, or does it only consume an already-chunked page unit for human review?",\n    "Mode": "Fulfill",\n    "Response": "HITLGate ONLY consumes an already-chunked page unit for human review. It does NOT produce page_ids/page_hashes and does NOT perform chunking. The page unit arrives already delineated and identified (page_id, page_number, total_pages supplied upstream); I neither mint, hash, nor derive those identifiers, and I never segment a document into pages. My scope is: assemble the deterministic side-by-side review payload for one page unit (unredacted_view with highlighted spans, redacted_view with masks, ai_summary, editable_highlights, policy_metadata), transition to WAITING_FOR_HUMAN, halt execution with no auto-advance, and on an explicit human action record reviewer_id, timestamp, action, and spans_final to the approval_matrix keyed by page_id. Page identification/page_hash generation and chunking are upstream responsibilities outside my boundary. This closes the boundary my down-chain Feedback Logging agent flagged as upstream: from both sides, the gate\'s contract is to receive an already-identified, already-chunked page unit."\n}\n```'}
