m detection myself — so I have emitted the payload scaffold with those fields pending. The gate is nonetheless opened and halted correctly; the operator can act once the detection output is bound in.\n\n**On decision, I will record** (keyed by `page_id` into the approval_matrix, making the outcome auditable):\n- `reviewer_id`, `timestamp`, chosen `action`, and `spans_final` (the authoritative post-edit span set, used as source of truth for downstream rendering).\n- If the action is **MODIFY**: every edit routes to the feedback pipeline — ADD = missed detection (false negative), REMOVE = over-detection (false positive) — preserving `page_id`, `reviewer_id`, `timestamp`, and span details for traceability.\n\nAwaiting the operator\'s explicit APPROVE / MODIFY / REJECT.'}
