2026-10-16 13:08:59 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-16 13:08:59 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent', 'active_learning_agent'], 'text': 'result from master_classifier_repository_agent\n{\n  "Name": "master_data_classifiers_governance_store",\n  "Inquiry": "Is a bare operator reply of \'Approved\' for page_id e3046c67146c169a77c17e8d239b2cadf27533d99bef3721fb442d5d803ee617 with NO bound upstream detection payload (unredacted_view / highlights / redacted_view / ai_summary all unpopulated) stored/treated as a valid structured human decision record in the feedback_buffer or governance store? What required per-decision fields (reviewer_id, timestamp, chosen action, spans_final) must be present, and can any learning signal be derived from an approval that lacks spans? Does the governance store hold decision/feedback records at all, or only the PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW proposal queue?",\n  "Mode": "Determine",\n  "Relevant": "Yes",\n  "Strength": 6,\n  "Claim": "Partial",\n  "Requirements": [\n    "Read access to the feedback_buffer / decision-record store (path not within my allowed_paths; I could confirm data/ exists but not read any store file, so its exact contents are unverified)",\n    "Confirmation of the bound upstream detection payload state for page_id e3046c67146c169a77c17e8d239b2cadf27533d99bef3721fb442d5d803ee617 (unredacted_view / highlights / redacted_view / ai_summary), which lives upstream of my ruleset authority",\n    "The owning agent of the feedback/learning pipeline to confirm the per-decision schema (reviewer_id, timestamp, chosen action, spans_final) actually enforced for feedback_buffer writes"\n  ],\n  "Response": "Scope split: within my authority I can answer the governance-store parts and fail closed on the rest.\\n\\n1) Valid structured human decision record? No. A bare \'Approved\' with no bound detection payload (unredacted_view / highlights / redacted_view / ai_summary all unpopulated) is not a valid structured decision record. It is an unbound acknowledgement: there is no referent span set to approve, so the decision cannot be verified, replayed, or attributed to a specific detection. Per my fail-closed rule, when decision validity, payload binding, or provenance cannot be confirmed, I treat the record as invalid rather than partial.\\n\\n2) Required per-decision fields: reviewer_id, timestamp (ISO-8601), chosen action (the explicit decision class), and spans_final (the finalized span set). Critically, spans_final must be bound to the upstream detection payload; an approval whose target spans are unpopulated leaves spans_final unresolvable, so the record is structurally incomplete even if the four field names are present. A missing payload binding is itself a required-field failure.\\n\\n3) Learning signal from a spans-less approval? No. Without spans there is no span-level supervision (no per-span label, no boundary, no confidence delta), so no classifier-learning signal can be derived. At most it is an aggregate page-level \'accepted\' event, which is not usable for updating span-type detection or confidence thresholds in the pinned ruleset. Deriving any signal from it would violate the rule against silently altering or expanding the ruleset.\\n\\n4) Does the governance store hold decision/feedback records? No — not in my holding. The governance store I am the system of record for contains only: (a) the pinned Master Data Classifiers ruleset (PII/PHI category hierarchy, regex span patterns, NER types, confidence thresholds) with its immutable versioned revisions and append-only change history, and (b) the PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW queue of unapproved proposals (with proposed change, origin, submission time). Reviewer decision/feedback records are the domain of the feedback_buffer, which is a separate store and outside my classifiers authority; I cannot confirm its schema or contents. A decision record is \'promoted\'/acted upon here only as an approved ruleset revision carrying a valid Human Admin token.\\n\\nIntegrity note: I attempted to read the governance store, feedback_buffer, and pending-review queue but the configured allow-list returned path_not_allowed for every candidate path (data/ exists but no store file was readable). I therefore cannot confirm the actual stored state and default to read-only, denying any write and treating the bare approval as not a valid decision record pending verification. No revision identifier can be cited because the active pinned ruleset revision could not be read."\n}'}
