nert by construction — never observable in the active ruleset — and holding is unconditional. Release, however, is gated on **token validity for that exact queued item**, not merely on a decision arriving: a decision with bound `spans_final` is necessary diff material but not by itself sufficient. If such a decision arrives without a verifying Human Admin token, it too is queued and nothing moves. Once a valid token for the exact item is presented, the store atomically assigns a new immutable revision, records actor, timestamp, token reference, and the diff, and appends history — supersession only, never erasure.\n\n**Caveat (fail-closed):** because store reads are currently blocked by the access allow-list, I cannot confirm from persisted state whether a PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW entry for this page_id already exists, nor cite the active pinned revision identifier. This response reflects the pinned governance boundary; re-issue the inspection once store read access is granted to obtain the exact revision ID and queue state.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "MasterDataClassifiersGovernanceStore",\n    "Inquiry": "Confirm governance-store boundary for a bare \'Approved\' decision on page_id e3046c67146c169a77c17e8d239b2cadf27533d99bef3721fb442d5d803ee617: does the store register such a record as a proposal in PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW, and would my learning pipeline emit ADD/REMOVE/ADJUST/CHANGE-threshold proposals derived from a spans-less approval? Please confirm you can hold STAGED proposals inert for this page if and only if a valid decision with bound spans_final arrives.",\n    "Mode": "Fulfill",\n    "Response": "Confirmed at the policy-boundary level. (1) A bare \'Approved\' decision is not a valid approval token; fail-closed applies — the write is rejected and the record is registered as a PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW proposal (origin-tagged, with page_id and submission time), leaving the active pinned revision untouched. (2) No ADD/REMOVE/ADJUST/CHANGE-threshold mutation can be derived or promoted from a spans-less approval: a versioned write requires a diff against the prior revision, and without bound spans_final there is no approvable diff; any such proposals from the learning pipeline are queued and stay inert. (3) STAGED proposals are held inert unconditionally; they can only be promoted when a valid Human Admin approval token verifies against the approval mechanism for that exact queued item — a decision with bound spans_final is required diff material but is not by itself sufficient for release. Caveat: store reads for this page_id returned path_not_allowed under the operator allow-list, so record-level queue state and the active pinned revision identifier could not be inspected or cited; no state was mutated."\n}\n```'}
