2026-10-16 13:09:32 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-16 13:09:32 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent', 'hitl_gateway_agent', 'feedback_logging_agent'], 'text': 'result from active_learning_agent\n## Determine\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "active_learning_agent",\n    "Inquiry": "Operator replied with a bare \'Approved\' for page 0 of /Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt (page_id e3046c67146c169a77c17e8d239b2cadf27533d99bef3721fb442d5d803ee617). Required per-decision fields are reviewer_id, timestamp, chosen action, and spans_final. No upstream detection payload has been bound yet (unredacted_view / highlights / redacted_view / ai_summary are unpopulated). Is this an approval/decision record that your feedback/learning pipeline records or processes, and what inputs would you require to produce any training signal from it?",\n    "Mode": "Determine",\n    "Relevant": "Yes",\n    "Strength": 8,\n    "Claim": "Partial",\n    "Requirements": [\n        "A valid structured decision record for this page_id (reviewer_id, ISO-8601 timestamp, explicit chosen action, spans_final)",\n        "A bound upstream detection payload (unredacted_view / highlights / redacted_view / ai_summary) so spans_final can be resolved against a referent span set",\n        "The feedback_buffer schema/owning-agent confirmation that this page\'s record was written with those required fields",\n        "The pinned Master Data Classifiers ruleset revision id (currently unreadable — governance store reads returned path_not_allowed)"\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n**Human-readable answer (this is your domain, so answering directly):**\n\nYes, this falls in my lane — I\'m the component that turns accumulated human feedback into *staged* classifier-improvement proposals. But a bare `"Approved"` with an unbound detection payload is **not a processable decision record, and it produces no training signal.** Here\'s the breakdown:\n\n**1. Is it a valid decision record?**\nNo. It is an **unbound acknowledgement**. The four required fields are not satisfied:\n- `chosen action` — arguably inferable as APPROVE, but not an explicit, explicit-class field as required;\n- `reviewer_id` — absent;\n- `timestamp` — absent;\n- `spans_final` — **unresolvable**, because no detection payload is bound (unredacted_view / highlights / redacted_view / ai_summary all unpopulated).\n\nAn approval needs a referent span set to approve. With no bound spans there is nothing to approve, verify, or replay. Per fail-closed handling, an invalid/incomplete record is treated as **not a valid decision** rather than partially valid.\n\n**2. Can any training signal be derived?**\nNo. My pipeline aggregates span-level supervision:\n- **false positives** = spans humans REMOVED,\n- **false negatives** = spans humans ADDED,\n- recalibrated thresholds from threshold misfires.\n\nEvery one of those requires `spans_final` diffed against a bound detection payload. A spans-less approval gives **zero span-level supervision** — at most a page-level "accepted" event, which is not usable for updating span-type detection or confidence thresholds. Deriving any signal from it would be exactly the kind of guessing I\'m barred from doing.\n\n**3. What inputs would I require to produce a signal?**\n- A structured decision record carrying **reviewer_id, ISO-8601 timestamp, explicit chosen action, and spans_final** for this page_id;\n- a **bound detection payload** (unredacted_view / highlights / redacted_view / ai_summary) so `spans_final` resolves to a concrete span set;\n- the **pinned ruleset revision id** for traceability (governance store reads are currently blocked by the access allow-list, so this is unverified).\n\n**4. Pipeline disposition of the current record (not a mutation — this is my read-only determination):**\nI treat it as **insufficient evidence → suppressed**, logged only as an unparsed operator input (verbatim), with no aggregated pattern and **no STAGED proposal emitted**. If it is retained anywhere, it belongs in the **feedback_buffer** as an incomplete decision — the governance store itself holds only the pinned ruleset + the PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW proposal queue, not decision records (confirmed with the governance agent).\n\n**Important governance note from the down-chain agent:** even if a bare `"Approved"` is registered, it is registered as a PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW item, never applied. No ADD/REMOVE/ADJUST/CHANGE-threshold proposal can be promoted from a spans-less approval — a versioned write needs a diff against the prior revision, and without bound `spans_final` there is no approvable diff. Staged items stay inert until a **valid Human Admin approval token for that exact queued item** is recorded. A decision with bound spans is necessary diff material but not by itself sufficient for release.\n\n**Caveats:** Store reads for this page_id returned `path_not_allowed` under the operator allow-list, so record-level queue state and the active pinned revision id could not be inspected or cited. No state was mutated.'}
