 require an exact `span` and a `context_snippet`. With **no upstream detection payload bound** (unredacted_view / highlights / redacted_view / ai_summary all unpopulated) and **no `spans_final`**, no span boundaries exist to record. There is nothing for me to persist durably — not even a null-span record, because the trigger condition (a human edit to a span) never occurred.\n\n**Inputs I would require to act at all:** an actual operator **edit** at the review gate carrying `page_id`, `change_type` (ADD/REMOVE), `classifier_id`, `category`, `context_snippet`, `span` offsets, `confidence`, `reviewer_id`, and an ISO-8601 `timestamp`. An unqualified approval supplies none of these.\n\n**Disposition:** the approval/decision record itself belongs to the **review-gate decision store / feedback buffer**, not to the feedback logging stage. I have written nothing, and correctly so.\n\n**Down-chain note:** I queried my down-chain `active_learning_agent`. It claims *partial* relevance (strength 8) — it can consume span-level supervision, but confirms that a spans-less approval with an unbound detection payload yields **zero span-level signal**, and that any such item enters its **PENDING_ADMIN_REVIEW** queue inert and never auto-applied. That confirms the practical path: route the decision record to the review gate / governance queue, and route only genuine span **edits** to me for durable logging.'}
