2026-10-16 13:09:41 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow - 2026-10-16 13:09:41 - generated/hitl_document_redaction_obfuscation_network - INFO - {'otrace': ['orchestrator_supervisor_agent'], 'text': 'result from hitl_gateway_agent\n## Follow up — HITL review-gate decision capture\n\n**Assessment: This is NOT a valid, recordable approval. It must not be written to the approval_matrix, and page 0 remains in WAITING_FOR_HUMAN.**\n\nThis inquiry sits squarely in my lane (HITL gate / decision capture), so here is the direct ruling.\n\n### 1. There is nothing to review, so there is nothing to approve\nThe gate protocol requires that a **side-by-side review payload be assembled and bound before a decision is solicited** — `unredacted_view` (text + highlights), `redacted_view` (text_with_masks), and `ai_summary` (num_spans, categories). Here, **no upstream detection payload has been bound**: all four fields are unpopulated. A decision cannot be validly rendered against an empty payload, because the human cannot have reviewed any spans. An approval of a payload that was never presented is not an approval of anything.\n\n### 2. Required per-decision fields are not satisfiable\n| Required field | Status from a bare "Approved" |\n|---|---|\n| `reviewer_id` | **Missing** — no identity binding; a bare token carries no reviewer attribution, so the record would be un-auditable. |\n| `timestamp` | **Missing** — not supplied. |\n| chosen action | Mappable to `APPROVE` in principle, but see below — it cannot be *consummated*. |\n| `spans_final` | **Undeterminable** — no highlight set was ever bound, so there is no authoritative post-edit span set to record. My protocol requires `spans_final` to be the source of truth for downstream rendering; an unbound payload yields an empty/undefined set. |\n\nA decision record missing 3 of 4 required fields — including the audit-critical `reviewer_id` — fails the recordability contract.\n\n### 3. No fabrication / no default approval\nI never infer, guess, or default an approval. A bare `"Approved"` is not an explicit, attributable human action against a *presented* payload, so I will not resolve the ambiguity myself by promoting it to a valid APPROVE. Escalation to the human, not self-resolution, is the correct move.\n\n### 4. Execution state\n- **No transition.** Execution stays in **WAITING_FOR_HUMAN** for `page_id e3046c67146c169a77c17e8d239b2cadf27533d99bef3721fb442d5d803ee617`.\n- **`auto_advance_on_timeout = false`** — with no valid decision, the gate simply holds. It does not advance.\n- **Nothing written** to the approval_matrix. No partial record, no null-span placeholder.\n\n### 5. Down-chain determination\nI queried `feedback_logging_agent` (my down-chain feedback stage). It returns **Relevant: No (strength 9)** — a bare approval is not a span ADD/REMOVE edit, so it produces no feedback record, and with no bound spans there is nothing to log as a false-negative/false-positive signal. This confirms the correct routing: this is a **decision-capture validity question**, not a feedback-logging one.\n\n### Required to make this recordable\nTo accept a valid APPROVE for this page, the operator decision must be preceded by a **bound review payload** (highlights + masks + ai_summary) and the decision must carry: `reviewer_id`, ISO-8601 `timestamp`, action = `APPROVE`, and `spans_final` (the authoritative span set for the page). Until those arrive, the record cannot and will not be written.\n\n```json\n{\n    "Name": "hitl_redaction_gate",\n    "Inquiry": "Operator replied with bare \'Approved\' for /Users/snigdhasahoo/Auto_Redaction/data/sample_pii_test_data.txt, page 0 (page_id e3046c67146c169a77c17e8d239b2cadf27533d99bef3721fb442d5d803ee617). Required fields: reviewer_id, timestamp, chosen action, spans_final. No upstream detection payload bound. Assess validity.",\n    "Mode": "Fulfill",\n    "Response": "INVALID / NOT RECORDABLE. No detection payload (unredacted_view, highlights, redacted_view, ai_summary) has been bound, so there was no presentable review payload and no human-reviewed spans. The decision is missing reviewer_id and timestamp, and spans_final is undeterminable (no bound highlight set). A bare \'Approved\' is not an explicit, attributable human action against a presented payload, so it cannot be defaulted or inferred into a valid APPROVE. No entry is written to the approval_matrix. Execution remains in WAITING_FOR_HUMAN with auto_advance_on_timeout=false; the gate holds without advancing. To record a valid approval, first bind the review payload, then supply reviewer_id, ISO-8601 timestamp, action=APPROVE, and spans_final as the authoritative post-edit span set. Down-chain feedback_logging_agent confirmed Not Relevant (strength 9): a spans-less approval is not a span ADD/REMOVE edit and yields no feedback record."\n}\n```'}
