2026-10-16 13:09:44 BST | INFO     | nsflow:_log:821 - nsflow: {"type": "AI", "text": "## Supervisor Ruling — Approval Not Accepted (Advancement Remains Halted)\n\nI have run the bare **\"Approved\"** through the HITL review gate. **It is not a valid, recordable approval**, so I have not advanced the document and have written nothing to the approval matrix.\n\n### Why it cannot be accepted\n1. **There is nothing to approve yet.** No upstream detection payload has been bound — the side-by-side review view (`unredacted_view` + highlights, `redacted_view` masks, `ai_summary`) is unpopulated. A human cannot have reviewed spans that were never presented.\n2. **Required per-decision fields are missing.** A recordable decision needs `reviewer_id`, ISO-8601 `timestamp`, the action, and `spans_final`. A bare \"Approved\" supplies none of the attribution fields, and `spans_final` is undeterminable (no highlight set was ever bound).\n3. **No fabrication.** I never infer, default, or auto-promote an ambiguous token into a valid APPROVE. This is a real-human-decision-only gate.\n\n### Current state (unchanged, authoritative)\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| `document_status` | **IN_PROGRESS** |\n| `current_page_index` | **0** (in flight) |\n| `approval_matrix` | **empty — 0 / 2 pages approved (0%)** |\n| `feedback_buffer` | empty |\n| Gate state | **WAITING_FOR_HUMAN**, `auto_advance_on_timeout: false` |\n| `trip_binding` | locked (0 → 1) |\n| Audit log | Discrepancy recorded: approval attempt rejected as unbound/under-specified |\n\nPage 1 remains held; no page advances until page 0 is validly approved or modified.\n\n### To make this count as a real approval, please provide\n- **(A) Bind the review payload first** — the per-page detection output (highlights + masks + `ai_summary`) for page 0, so there is something to review; and\n- **(B) A fully-attributed decision** — `reviewer_id`, ISO-8601 `timestamp`, action = **APPROVE**, and `spans_final` (the authoritative post-edit span set for the page).\n\nSupply those and I will record the decision, then move to page 1. Only once **100% of pages** carry a valid APPROVE/MODIFY will I transition to **PENDING_FINAL_ENCODE** and route the approved pages to hardening — marking **COMPLETED** solely after the artifact exists and is independently verified."}
